// @ens-test
// @exit 1
// @stdout-contains PASS first test passes
// @stderr-contains panic: boom
// @stderr-contains The test run ended unexpectedly
// @stderr-contains while running test 'second test panics'
// @stderr-contains crash_test.ens
// @stderr-contains 1 of 2 tests had reported a result
// A panic in the second test aborts the whole run. The first result still
// survives (it was flushed) on standard output, the panic reaches standard error
// straight from the runner, and the report there names the test that was running
// when the run ended plus how many results came before it.
